Port Geminum Orbis r59 to native ncurses on GNU/Linux.

Upstream: https://svn.code.sf.net/p/adventurerpg/code/trunk/ (revision 59)
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [platform port of inactive upstream]

The author's public-domain dedication is recorded at RogueBasin revision
24451 (2011-04-21); SourceForge also records the project under GPLv2:
https://roguebasin.com/api.php?action=compare&format=json&fromrev=24448&torev=24451
https://sourceforge.net/rest/p/adventurerpg/
This patch is released under the same public-domain dedication, with GPLv2
as an alternative permission.

Remove Win32/conio dependencies and unused console helpers.  Let curses
manage the terminal, check the actual 80x25 minimum instead of attempting
to resize a Windows console buffer, and restore the terminal on errors.
Map PDCurses bright colors to the standard eight curses colors plus bold;
check color capabilities and every init_pair result.  Replace active CP437
byte strings with curses graphics (and the map's own fountain symbol), so
map cells remain single-column glyphs rather than malformed UTF-8 bytes.

Promote the random range width before multiplying by rand(): glibc's
larger RAND_MAX otherwise overflows the upstream int multiplication.
Keep the original inclusive range and RAND_MAX + 1.0 scaling.

Fix bare refresh/endwin expressions and the missing quit-confirmation
braces.  Draw_Tile has no return value or value-using callers, so declare
it void instead of falling off a non-void function.  Leave upstream's
unimplemented saving and all maps and game features intact.  Read the two
original maps from GEMINUM_DATA_DIR, independently of the writable current
directory used by the upstream highscores file.
Skip CR bytes in both map parsers, matching Windows text-mode reads while
preserving the original CRLF map files and existing LF row logic.

